<section class="block">
<h2>Who this is for</h2>
<p>The UAE is moving quickly on AI and digital services, and many organisations here need senior technical leadership faster than they can hire it. I work with:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Founders and scale-ups</strong> in Dubai and Abu Dhabi who need a CTO-level partner for architecture, hiring and investor conversations.</li>
<li><strong>Enterprises and family groups</strong> modernising legacy systems and setting an AI strategy that will stand up to scrutiny.</li>
<li><strong>Healthcare and regulated organisations</strong> that need to use sensitive data responsibly and keep it in-country.</li>
<li><strong>Investors and funds</strong> that want an independent technical view before they commit capital.</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section class="block">
<h2>The problems I solve</h2>
<h3>AI strategy that turns into delivery</h3>
<p>Many AI programmes in the region start with ambition and a vendor shortlist. I help pick the use cases that pay back, ground them in your own data and get one into production with evaluation and cost controls. The detail is on my <a href="/ai-architect/">AI and LLM architecture</a> page.</p>
<h3>Data protection and residency</h3>
<p>Companies may fall under the federal Personal Data Protection Law, or under the separate DIFC or ADGM data-protection regimes if they are based in those free zones, along with sector rules and customer expectations about where data lives. I design architecture that maps data flows, keeps regulated data in the right place and records who accessed what. I work alongside your legal advisers, who interpret the law; my job is to make the systems match their advice.</p>
<h3>Private AI for sensitive data</h3>
<p>When data cannot leave the country, or the building, I design private AI setups: in-country cloud regions, on-prem open-weight models and gateways that route by sensitivity. I wrote more about this in <a href="/insights/private-llm-on-prem/">running private LLMs on-prem</a>.</p>
<h3>Leadership gaps</h3>
<p>Senior technical hires take time. A <a href="/fractional-cto/">fractional CTO</a> gives you that judgement now and helps you hire the permanent leader.</p>
</section>
<section class="block">
<h2>My approach</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Understand the business and the regulatory context.</strong> Free zone or mainland, sector rules, customer commitments.</li>
<li><strong>Map data and systems.</strong> What you hold, where it lives, how it moves and who can see it.</li>
<li><strong>Set the target architecture and roadmap.</strong> Cloud, data, AI and security decisions tied to business milestones.</li>
<li><strong>Deliver a first production win.</strong> One use case, measured and governed.</li>
<li><strong>Build the team.</strong> Hiring, mentoring and an operating rhythm that works across time zones.</li>
</ol>
</section>
<section class="block">
<h2>What you get</h2>
<ul>
<li>A technology and AI roadmap your board can act on.</li>
<li>A data map and residency design aligned with your legal advice.</li>
<li>Reference architecture for cloud, data platform and AI, with security built in.</li>
<li>A working AI pilot with evaluation, guardrails and cost tracking.</li>
<li>Hiring plans and role definitions for senior technical staff.</li>
<li>Technical due diligence reports for investment decisions. See <a href="/technical-due-diligence/">technical due diligence</a>.</li>
</ul>
</section>
