<section class="block">
<h2>Why a regional view matters</h2>
<p>Much of the advice written about AI and data assumes a US or European regulatory setting and US-hosted cloud services. In the UAE the picture is different in a few practical ways.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>More than one data-protection regime.</strong> Mainland companies, DIFC entities and ADGM entities can face different rules, and groups often span several of them.</li>
<li><strong>Residency expectations.</strong> Government, healthcare and financial customers frequently expect data to stay in the country, which shapes cloud region choice and AI vendor choice.</li>
<li><strong>Arabic and English together.</strong> Search, retrieval and AI assistants often need to work across both languages, which affects model selection and evaluation.</li>
<li><strong>Fast-moving national AI agenda.</strong> Expectations from boards and regulators are rising quickly, so governance has to be designed in, not added later.</li>
</ul>
<p>I bring architecture patterns proven at scale, adapted to these constraints, and I am clear about where legal advice is needed and where engineering decisions can move ahead.</p>
</section>
<section class="block">
<h2>Typical first projects</h2>
<ul>
<li>An AI readiness review that ranks use cases and sets a governance baseline.</li>
<li>A data map and residency plan for a group spanning mainland and free-zone entities.</li>
<li>A private AI pilot on in-country or on-prem infrastructure for sensitive documents.</li>
<li>Technical due diligence on a regional acquisition or growth investment.</li>
<li>Fractional CTO cover while a scale-up hires its first permanent technology leader.</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section class="block">
<h2>Working across time zones</h2>
<p>Gulf teams often work with suppliers, investors or parent companies in the US and Europe. I keep a fixed weekly overlap for live sessions, write decisions down so nobody has to be on every call, and use short recorded walkthroughs for reviews. That rhythm keeps momentum without asking anyone to work at midnight, and it suits groups with offices in Dubai, Abu Dhabi and abroad.</p>
</section>
